{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Spike7aParent",
    "description": "PLAN.md step 7a, the parent half, in the ONE spelling that evaluates under BOTH bindings. This document holds no model and no shape of its own: two `data_sources` and a single top-level `models` entry that is a `{ref}`. `age_group_census.esm` supplies every variable, every equation, every data BINDING, its own shape, and the metaparameters that size it; nothing here names a column, an axis or an arithmetic operation.\n\nWHAT 7a ESTABLISHES. A variable declared inside a ref'd child CAN carry `update: {kind: \"data\", source: \"X\"}` where `data_sources.X` is declared only in the mounting document. That is §7.1's load-bearing assumption and it holds: the two Parquet files are read, the equi-join runs, and the numbers are the default database's own (41 categories in 7 groups, ageIDs summing to 820, group 2099 holding 21). The child fails alone — it reads two sources it does not declare — and evaluates through this parent, which is §7.2's probe carried the one step further that §7.5 said was missing.\n\nTHE SHAPE MOVED TWICE AND THE NUMBERS DID NOT. As first written this document also declared the two `index_sets` that size the child's axes, and the child declared them open — sized by names only this file provided. EarthSciAST PR #298 (2026-09-12) resolves a mounted leaf in its own scope and refuses that; the Python binding had been refusing it all along, as `subsystem_index_set_conflict`, while Rust accepted it (finding F51). So the axes and the metaparameters that size them moved into the child — and this file kept a copy of the two metaparameters, because the loader API bound discovered extents only at the ROOT and refused a root that declared none (finding F50). EarthSciAST PR #317 (2026-09-14) binds a discovered extent in whichever document of the assembly declares the name, so that copy is gone too, and F50 is retired. The emitted relation is unchanged through both moves.\n\nTHREE THINGS §7.2 DID NOT SAY, each measured here and filed. Two have since been overtaken, and are kept because the workarounds they forced are traceable through them.\n\n1. THE PARENT USED TO HAVE TO RESTATE THE CHILD'S `index_sets`. Without them `esm validate` PASSED and the build failed with `aggregate range 'g' references index set 'spike_agegroup_rows', which is not declared in the document index_sets registry`, because the interpreter's registry is `file.index_sets` — this document's own — and a mounted child's did not enter it. That was finding F46, and PR #298 closed it: there is no `index_sets` block in this file any more.\n\n2. THIS DOCUMENT MAY NOT HOLD A MODEL OF ITS OWN. Add one — an asserting model, in the F21 shape, doing nothing but `parentTotalAge = AgeGroupCensus.totalAge` — and every assertion in the document errors with `document holds several models; pass model_name`. The ingesting build takes exactly one model and `--model` narrows the report without reaching the build. Finding F45. So the mount is the whole of `models`, and per-fixture assertions cannot be inline.\n\n3. A MOUNTED CHILD'S `data_sources` MERGE UP, AND ITS `extent`-BOUND METAPARAMETERS NO LONGER NEED TO BE RESTATED. The `data_sources` half is what lets a shared domain document carry the whole default-database catalogue while each fixture adds only its own runspec sources. The metaparameter half was finding F50: until EarthSciAST PR #317 the two names had to be declared here as well as in the child, because this document's `extent`s bind them and the loader API closed discovered extents only at the root; `bindings` could not bridge it, since it closes a name the child declares and cannot supply one it lacks. They are declared once now, in the child that owns the axes.\n\nTHE PATH IS ABSOLUTE AND MACHINE-LOCAL, deliberately. The default database is 1.1 GB and is not in this repository, so a `url_template` naming it cannot be repository-relative the way a snapshot path can. run-tests.sh SKIPS the spike stage when the directory is absent rather than failing it, which is how the fixture stage already treats a missing snapshot corpus.\n\nHOW THIS IS CHECKED. `run-tests.sh` emits this document's relation with `simulate --format csv` and diffs it against `expected/age_group_census.csv`, which is the fixture stage's own emit-and-compare pattern and the only verification F45 leaves available. It also asserts that `esm test` on this file finds ZERO assertions, so the day a mounted child's inline tests do run (finding F47) the suite says so instead of the diff silently remaining the weaker check. There is no metaparameter probe any more: until F50 was fixed the stage deleted this file's `metaparameters` block into a probe and required the build to refuse it, and this file is now exactly that probe's shape, so the diff is the check that the fix holds.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["moves", "spike", "phase7", "run"]
  },

  "data_sources": {
    "spike_agecategory": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": { "url_template": "file:///scratch/ctessum/movesdb/movesdb20241112/AgeCategory.parquet" },
      "extent": { "metaparameter": "n_spike_agecategory" },
      "metadata": { "tags": ["default-db"], "note": "41 rows. The default database's agecategory table, unmodified and read in place.", "esio_format": "parquet" }
    },
    "spike_agegroup": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": { "url_template": "file:///scratch/ctessum/movesdb/movesdb20241112/AgeGroup.parquet" },
      "extent": { "metaparameter": "n_spike_agegroup" },
      "metadata": { "tags": ["default-db"], "note": "7 rows. The default database's agegroup table, unmodified and read in place.", "esio_format": "parquet" }
    }
  },

  "models": {
    "AgeGroupCensus": { "ref": "./age_group_census.esm" }
  }
}
